# copilot — copied to host-only secrets/copilot.env by install.sh / scaffolded
# by mint-secrets.sh on deploy. Neither value is auto-minted: both are
# operator-supplied credentials the seat cannot generate for itself.
#
# The operator's Anthropic SUBSCRIPTION token — flat-rate Opus/Sonnet, NOT a
# metered API key. Generate on a trusted machine with `claude setup-token`
# (one-time; it prints a long-lived token), then paste the value here.
# require: run `claude setup-token` on a trusted machine and paste the token here
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Forgejo token for the `copilot` user: write:issue + write:repository. Branch
# protection on main keeps merge (= deploy authorization) with the operator, so
# this is a PROPOSER credential, never a merge/deploy one. Do NOT grant it
# organization/admin scope: Forgejo performs mirror fetches server-side, so a
# token with `mirrors`-org write would let the copilot mirror arbitrary repos
# via the migrate API — an egress bypass around the Anthropic-only allowlist.
# require: mint a Forgejo token for the `copilot` user (scopes: write:issue, write:repository — NOT org/admin)
COPILOT_FORGEJO_TOKEN=
# NOTE: the headroom token-optimizer (copilot-headroom) needs NO credential of
# its own — it forwards the copilot's subscription OAuth header transparently.
# Tuning (e.g. --mode token) is a one-line edit in apps/copilot/compose.yaml,
# not a secret. See docs/COPILOT.md "Token cost: the headroom optimizer".
